<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ariarathes II of Cappadocia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 280 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ariarathes II was the adopted son of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrap</a> Ariarathes I, who restored his family's rule in Cappadocia after his father's execution in 322 BCE. Around 301 BCE, with Armenian help, he drove out the Macedonian governor and re-established an independent principality in the region. His heirs later took the title king.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ariarathes-ii-of-cappadocia.jpg" alt="Ariarathes II of Cappadocia" width="320" height="151" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KINGS_of_CAPPADOCIA._Ariarathes_II._Circa_301-280_BC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
